<title>FRANCE: MATIF commodities volume drops in November.</title>
<headline>MATIF commodities volume drops in November.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of commodities futures and options traded on the French MATIF exchange in November fell 29.8 percent from the previous month and 23.2 percent from November 1995, MATIF said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures were as follows,</p>
<p>		   Volume     Change	Change     Open Positions</p>
<p>				  on month    on year	at end-month</p>
<p>All contracts   20,424     -29.8	 -23.2	  13,655</p>
<p>Total futures   20,224     -30.0	 -24.0	  13,205</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p> White sugar($) 15,269     -11.4	 -26.4	   6,217</p>
<p> Potatoes	    698     175.9	 -42.0	     667</p>
<p> Rapeseed	  2,702     -72.4	 -41.9	   5,302</p>
<p> Wheat	     1,555	-3.7	   NA	    1,019</p>
<p> Sugar options     200	 0.0	   NA		450</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
